  "description": "107 Magdalen Road PD",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal constitutes development under the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, and the local planning authority is not satisfied that, based on the drawings submitted as part of the application, this proposal falls within any class of 'permitted development' specified within Schedule 2 to the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).\r\nINFORMATIVE: The proposed development fails to comply with condition (j) (iii) and (ja) of Class A, condition (d) (i) and conditions (a), (d) of Class B, of Part 1, Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) as the proposal would extend beyond a wall forming a side elevation of the original dwellinghouse and would have width greater than half the width of the original dwelling house; its new additional volume at roof level would exceed 40m3; the proposed materials used in exterior work would not be of a similar appearance to those used in the construction of the exterior of the existing dwellinghouse (rear dormer); and the new window inserted on a wall forming a side elevation of the dwellinghouse (at 2nd floor level) would not be obscured and openable 1.7m above internal floor level only."
  ],
